  "body": "## Cause\r\n\r\nPR #3421 (#3300) changed the 5-axis stamp: a path that leans states the upright Z column on each station before its first lean. Three motion tests pinned the old law (\"no pose before the first lean\"). The gate of #3421 did not run these three binaries.\r\n\r\n## Panic texts (origin/main fd64cc2f5, debug)\r\n\r\n- `multiaxis.rs:180` `rapids_hold_the_pose_they_inherit`: `a rapid changed the pose it inherited: Move { kind: Rapid, from: (0, 0, 20), to: (4.919, -8.452, 20), axis: Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0]) }` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\r\n- `multiaxis_avoid.rs:176` `dodging_never_moves_the_ball`: `a rapid changed the pose it inherited` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\r\n- `multiaxis_rough.rs:161` `rapids_and_floors_hold_no_pose_and_flanks_do`: `a rapid changed the pose it inherited` - left `Some([0.0, 0.0, 1.0])`, right `None`.\r\n\r\n## Product or test: test, for all three\r\n\r\n- Each failure is the opening rapid at the clearance, before the first lean.\r\n- Each test starts its \"inherited pose\" memory at `None`. The stamp itself holds the upright home there (`held = UP`, stamp.rs). The rapid states the pose that it inherits from the home. It does not state a new angle.\r\n- After the first lean, the stamp rule is unchanged: a rapid holds `held` (the last lean), and a cut states its lean or the upright Z column. The #3300 fill touches only `None` poses, and these exist only before the first lean. So no rapid states upright while the machine is tilted.\r\n- Each stamp caller (`contour5d`, `parallel5d`, `flow5d`, `multiaxis_rough`, `swarf`) stamps the whole path one time. No caller joins two stamped paths, so an upright opening never follows a lean inside one path.\r\n- Multi-Axis Rough floors: before the first lean they now state the upright Z column; after it they state it too (that was already the law: `lean.or(Some(UP))`). The rule is now the same on both sides of the first lean. The post writes A0 B0 one time on the first stated move of a section that leans. Later upright moves before a lean write no word, and after a lean the existing zero-return rule applies.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\nOnly the three tests. Each test now:\r\n- starts the inherited-pose memory at the upright home `Some([0, 0, 1])`;\r\n- asserts that the path leans, so that the law applies (`multiaxis_rough` proves the lean with its flank count);\r\n- keeps the strict `assert_eq!` for each rapid.\r\n\r\nNo assertion is weaker, and no test is ignored. No product code changed.\r\n\r\n## Gate results (debug, this head)\r\n\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion -j 6 --no-fail-fast`: 136 test binaries (incl. lib and doc), all `test result: ok`:\r\n  - lib: `ok. 538 passed; 0 failed; 10 ignored`\r\n  - `multiaxis`: `ok. 7 passed; 0 failed`\r\n  - `multiaxis_avoid`: `ok. 6 passed; 0 failed`\r\n  - `multiaxis_rough`: `ok. 5 passed; 0 failed`\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## What the red run did not reach\r\n\r\nNothing. Post-merge run 45036812289 on c31384ae4 ran all 1092 steps: 1089 ok, 3 FAIL (the three above), none skipped. So all app, post, sim and ui suites of the batch tier were green on the merge of #3421. This PR changes only motion test files, so I did not build the app. The heavy lanes of #3421 ran green on its head (242 steps, 0 failed; see #3421).\r\n\r\nNot run here: the app binaries (not touched; green in the run above), the heavy lanes (no product change).\r\n\r\nOverlap: PR #3478 (#3466) has base `main` now and changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps`, `assets/posts/doosan-dnm.cps`, a new post test and its decision file. It does not change `stamp.rs`, `post/mod.rs` or these three tests. No overlap with this PR. It needs no change for this fix.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none\r\n\r\nFixes #3486\r\nRefs #3300\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
